# listed = Float64Array.of(1, 2.5);  mapped = Uint8Array.from(source, half);  either = (flag ? Int16Array : Int32Array).of(1);  made = Float64Array.of.call(Maker, 1)
# marked = Uint16Array.of(1); marked.slice = 1;  other = Uint16Array.of(2)
# `of` and `from` answer what their receiver constructs. Where the receiver is a constructor of the table, native code makes the call, and what it makes has the class of that constructor,
# and the names and the storage it was made with as long as the program does nothing to any of them. Two constructors make two classes. A function of the program makes whatever it likes.
# One object stands for all that native code makes with one constructor: what is done to one of them counts for all.
# RUN: valueflow-apply
# CHECK: variable g0 name="listed" {{*}}declared={type=Float64Array<anything, pristine[Storage, Names]>}
# CHECK: variable g1 name="mapped" {{*}}declared={type=Uint8Array<anything, pristine[Storage, Names]>}
# CHECK: variable g2 name="either" {{*}}declared={type=Int16Array<anything, pristine[Storage, Names]>|Int32Array<anything, pristine[Storage, Names]>}
# CHECK: variable g3 name="made" {{*}}declared={type=anything}
# CHECK: variable g4 name="marked" {{*}}declared={type=Uint16Array<anything, pristine[Storage]>}
# CHECK: variable g5 name="other" {{*}}declared={type=Uint16Array<anything, pristine[Storage]>}

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
variable g0 name="listed" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
variable g1 name="mapped" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
variable g2 name="either" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
variable g3 name="made" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
variable g4 name="marked" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
variable g5 name="other" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=Float64Array
    v1 = Builtin builtin=TypedArrayOf
    v2 = Integer integer=1
    v3 = Double number=2.5
    v4 = Call v1, v0, v2, v3
    PutModuleVariable v4 variable=g0
    v6 = Builtin builtin=Uint8Array
    v7 = Builtin builtin=TypedArrayFrom
    v8 = NewArray v2, v2
    v9 = NewClosure function=f1
    v10 = Call v7, v6, v8, v9
    PutModuleVariable v10 variable=g1
    v12 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v13 = PropGet v12 key="flag" [isFreeName]
    v14 = ToBoolean v13
    Branch v14 -> taken b1(), notTaken b2()
  b1():
    v15 = Builtin builtin=Int16Array
    Jump -> next b3(v15)
  b2():
    v16 = Builtin builtin=Int32Array
    Jump -> next b3(v16)
  b3(v17):
    v18 = Call v1, v17, v2
    PutModuleVariable v18 variable=g2
    v20 = NewClosure function=f2
    v21 = Call v1, v20, v2
    PutModuleVariable v21 variable=g3
    v23 = Builtin builtin=Uint16Array
    v24 = Call v1, v23, v2
    PropSet v24, v2 key="slice" mode=Strict
    PutModuleVariable v24 variable=g4
    v27 = Call v1, v23, v2
    PutModuleVariable v27 variable=g5
    Return v4
}
function f1 name="half" kind=Arrow parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0):
    v1 = Integer integer=2
    v2 = Div v0, v1
    Return v2
}
function f2 name="Maker" parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0):
    v1 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v2 = PropGet v1 key="other" [isFreeName]
    Return v2
}
